1. Intern a column: eight values, three distinct
   symbols               [0, 1, 0, 2, 1, 0, 2, 0]
   texts stored          3
   owners of each text   2 (the map's key and the Vec's entry)

2. Handles compare as integers, and are small
   symbols[0] == symbols[2], both Ada   true
   a Symbol                             4 bytes
   a &str                               2 machine words

3. Resolve when the text is needed, as many at once as you like
   Ada, Ben, Cara
   resolve takes &self, so three shared borrows can be alive together.

4. Why intern does not hand out &str
   fn intern(&mut self, s: &str) -> &str ties the &str it returns to the
   MUTABLE borrow of the interner. Keep the first result and call intern
   again, and rustc stops with E0499: two mutable borrows at once.
   A Symbol borrows nothing, so that question never comes up.
